@startuml class_diagram_spa
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing true
skinparam linetype ortho

title Class Diagram (Design) - WEB06 Kitchen Configuration Page (Front-End SPA)

' -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
' component = React component (function), module = plain JS module,
' record = shape of a JavaScript object, existing = delivered by another story.
' -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
package "Front-End (SPA)" <<Rectangle>> {

    package "kitchen (WEB06) - frontend/src/kitchen" <<Rectangle>> {

        class KitchenConfigurationsModule <<component>> {
            + props.request : ModuleRequest
            + render() : Routes
        }
        note right of KitchenConfigurationsModule
            Default export loaded lazily by ModulePage
            (WEB01) for the "kitchenConfigurations" entry.
            Nested routes (all MANAGER, inherited from
            the WEB03 section "kitchen-configurations"):
              index           -> KitchenConfigurationListPage
              new             -> KitchenConfigurationEditorPage
              :configurationId -> KitchenConfigurationDetailPage
            Builds ONE kitchenConfigurationApi from
            props.request and passes it down.
        end note

        class kitchenConfigurationApi <<module>> {
            + createKitchenConfigurationApi(request) : KitchenConfigurationApi
            + list(signal) : Summary[]
            + getById(id, signal) : Detail
            + getActive(signal) : ActiveConfiguration
            + create({ name, content }) : Detail
            + update(id, { name, content, version }) : Detail
            + remove(id) : null
            + activate(id) : ActivationResult
            + validate(content) : ValidationReport
            + listAssets(signal) : KitchenAsset[]
        }
        note right of kitchenConfigurationApi
            HTTP adapter (WEB01 convention): one function
            per endpoint, DTO in / DTO out, ids encoded
            with encodeURIComponent, no cache, no rules.
            getActive() is the SAME contract used by the
            VIS01 viewer (it has its own adapter call).
        end note

        class configurationJson <<module>> {
            + parseConfigurationText(text) : ParseResult
            + formatConfiguration(value) : string
            + readImportFile(file : File) : Promise<ImportedFile>
            + MAX_IMPORT_BYTES = 100 KB
        }
        note bottom of configurationJson
            Pure functions (unit-tested without React).
            parseConfigurationText: JSON.parse + line /
            column of a syntax error; top level must be
            an object.
            readImportFile: only ".json", <= 100 KB, UTF-8;
            never sends anything by itself.
        end note

        class ParseResult <<record>> {
            + ok : boolean
            + value? : object
            + error? : { line, column, message }
        }

        class ImportedFile <<record>> {
            + suggestedName : string
            + text : string
        }

        class KitchenConfigurationListPage <<component>> {
            - configurations : Summary[]
            - state : "loading" | "ready" | "empty" | "error"
            - activationNotice : ActivationResult | null
            + onActivate(summary) : void
            + onDelete(summary) : void
        }
        note right of KitchenConfigurationListPage
            Re-reads the list after every successful
            change (WEB05 / WEB01 BR 14).
            Delete is disabled for the ACTIVE row
            (the back end also rejects it with 409).
        end note

        class KitchenConfigurationEditorPage <<component>> {
            + props.mode : "create" | "edit"
            + props.initial : Detail | null
            - name : string
            - text : string
            - version : number | null
            - syntaxError : SyntaxPosition | null
            - issues : ValidationIssue[]
            - submitting : boolean
            - concurrency : ConcurrencyState
            + onImport(file) : void
            + onValidate() : void
            + onSave() : void
            + onReloadLatest() : void
            + onResolveConflict(path, choice) : void
            + onContinueWithRebased() : void
            + onDiscardMyDraft() : void
            + onAcknowledgeReview(checked) : void
        }
        note right of KitchenConfigurationEditorPage
            The typed / imported text is KEPT after any
            failure (WEB04 AC 5). Save and Validate are
            disabled while a request is in progress.
            base = record as loaded (kept all session).
            409 (stale version) -> phase "conflict":
            draft = { name, text } kept, Save disabled,
            "Reload latest version" offered (SD 2).
            After reload: rebaseDraft(base, draft, latest)
            -> the save is built on latest; only the
            Manager's own changes are re-applied.
            Save is enabled again only in phase
            "reviewing" with every conflict resolved and
            reviewAcknowledged = true; the next PUT sends
            the rebased content with latest.version.
            Language (BR 21): all of this is React state
            of this page; the route is not keyed by
            language and no effect depends on it, so a
            PT/EN switch only re-renders the texts.
        end note

        class ConcurrencyState <<record>> {
            + phase : "none" | "conflict" | "reviewing"
            + base : { name, content, version }
            + draft : { name, text } | null
            + latest : Detail | null
            + rebase : RebaseResult | null
            + resolutions : Map<path, "mine" | "theirs">
            + reviewAcknowledged : boolean
        }

        class ConcurrentChangePanel <<component>> {
            + props.draft : { name, text }
            + props.latest : Detail | null
            + props.rebase : RebaseResult | null
            + props.resolutions : Map<path, choice>
            + props.reviewAcknowledged : boolean
            + onReloadLatest() : void
            + onResolveConflict(path, choice) : void
            + onContinueWithRebased() : void
            + onDiscardMyDraft() : void
            + onAcknowledgeReview(checked) : void
        }
        note bottom of ConcurrentChangePanel
            "This configuration was changed by another
            user (now version N, <updatedAt>)."
            Lists the other user's changes (kept), the
            Manager's changes re-applied on the latest
            version and every conflict with
            [Keep mine] / [Keep theirs].
            Save needs all conflicts resolved AND the
            checkbox "I reviewed the other user's changes".
            The whole draft is never sent over latest.
        end note

        class compareConfigurations <<module>> {
            + compareConfigurations(from, to) : ChangeSet
        }
        note bottom of compareConfigurations
            Pure function. One change per path:
            /name; every leaf outside elements
            (e.g. /content/kitchen/dimensions/width);
            elements matched BY ID: added, removed, or
            changed leaves (/content/elements[id]/...).
            Other arrays compared as a whole.
        end note

        class ChangeSet <<record>> {
            + changes : Change[]
        }

        class Change <<record>> {
            + path : string
            + kind : "set" | "add" | "remove"
            + before : any
            + after : any
        }

        class rebaseDraft <<module>> {
            + rebaseDraft(base, draft, latest) : RebaseResult
            + applyResolutions(result, resolutions) : RebaseResult
        }
        note bottom of rebaseDraft
            Pure three-way rebase (D16):
            candidate = copy of latest; for each change of
            compareConfigurations(base, draft):
            - no change of (base -> latest) on the same or an
              overlapping path -> applied to candidate
            - same value -> nothing to do
            - different value -> Conflict (Manager decides)
            New draft elements appended after latest's.
            Draft not parseable -> "rebase-impossible".
        end note

        class RebaseResult <<record>> {
            + candidate : { name, content }
            + applied : Change[]
            + theirs : Change[]
            + conflicts : Conflict[]
        }

        class Conflict <<record>> {
            + path : string
            + base : any
            + mine : any
            + theirs : any
        }

        class KitchenConfigurationDetailPage <<component>> {
            + props.configurationId : string
            - detail : Detail | null
            - editing : boolean
        }

        class ActiveConfigurationBanner <<component>> {
            + props.active : Summary | null
            + props.loadError : ApiError | null
            + onOpenViewer() : void
        }
        note bottom of ActiveConfigurationBanner
            "Active: <name> (<id>)" + "Open / reload
            the kitchen viewer" (navigates to
            /kitchen/viewer, which re-reads the
            active configuration on mount).
            No active one -> explicit warning;
            never a default layout.
        end note

        class JsonContentEditor <<component>> {
            + props.value : string
            + props.onChange(text) : void
            + props.syntaxError : SyntaxPosition | null
            + props.readOnly : boolean
        }

        class ValidationIssueList <<component>> {
            + props.issues : ValidationIssue[]
        }
        note bottom of ValidationIssueList
            One row per issue: JSON path, message
            (i18n by code + params, WEB02) - announced
            with role="alert" for screen readers.
            Messages are derived from codes at render
            time, so a language switch re-translates
            them without losing the issues (BR 21).
        end note

        class ActivationConfirmDialog <<component>> {
            + props.target : Summary
            + props.currentActive : Summary | null
        }
        class DeleteConfirmDialog <<component>> {
            + props.target : Summary
        }
    }

    package "Shared (existing / extended)" <<Rectangle>> {

        class ModulePage <<existing WEB01>> {
            + props.roles : UserRole[]
            + props.load : () => Promise<Module>
        }
        class ModuleRequest <<existing WEB01>> {
            + request(method, path, { body, query, signal })
        }
        note bottom of ModuleRequest
            Session-bound: adds the bearer token and
            re-checks /auth/me after a 401 / 403
            (WEB01 SD 3 / WEB03 SD 3).
        end note
        class apiClient <<existing WEB01>> {
            + request(method, path, options)
        }
        class ApiError <<extended>> {
            + status : number
            + kind : string
            + message : string
            + details : ValidationIssue[] | undefined
        }
        note bottom of ApiError
            ALN-2: copies error.details from a 4xx
            body (array of { path, code, message }).
        end note
        class moduleRoutes <<extended WEB01>> {
            + kitchenConfigurations : { path, roles: [MANAGER] }
        }
        class navigationPolicy <<extended WEB03>> {
            + "kitchen-configurations" : enabled = true
        }
        class LanguageContext <<WEB02>> {
            + language : "pt" | "en"
            + t(key, params) : string
        }
        note bottom of LanguageContext
            Selection persisted by WEB02 across
            navigation, refreshes and visits.
            Changing it re-renders consumers only.
        end note
        class ConfirmDialog <<WEB04>>
        class LoadingIndicator <<WEB04>>
        class FeedbackMessage <<WEB04>>
    }
}

ModulePage ..> KitchenConfigurationsModule : lazy load,\npasses request
moduleRoutes ..> ModulePage
navigationPolicy ..> moduleRoutes : same path / roles
KitchenConfigurationsModule ..> kitchenConfigurationApi : creates with request
kitchenConfigurationApi --> ModuleRequest
ModuleRequest --> apiClient
apiClient ..> ApiError : throws

KitchenConfigurationsModule --> KitchenConfigurationListPage
KitchenConfigurationsModule --> KitchenConfigurationEditorPage
KitchenConfigurationsModule --> KitchenConfigurationDetailPage
KitchenConfigurationDetailPage --> KitchenConfigurationEditorPage : edit mode
KitchenConfigurationListPage --> ActiveConfigurationBanner
KitchenConfigurationListPage --> ActivationConfirmDialog
KitchenConfigurationListPage --> DeleteConfirmDialog
KitchenConfigurationEditorPage --> JsonContentEditor
KitchenConfigurationEditorPage --> ValidationIssueList
KitchenConfigurationEditorPage *-- ConcurrencyState
KitchenConfigurationEditorPage --> ConcurrentChangePanel : phase != "none"
KitchenConfigurationEditorPage ..> compareConfigurations
compareConfigurations ..> ChangeSet
ChangeSet *-- Change
KitchenConfigurationEditorPage ..> rebaseDraft
rebaseDraft ..> compareConfigurations
rebaseDraft ..> RebaseResult
RebaseResult *-- Conflict
ConcurrentChangePanel --> JsonContentEditor : read-only (latest)
KitchenConfigurationEditorPage ..> LanguageContext : t()
ValidationIssueList ..> LanguageContext : t(code, params)
ConcurrentChangePanel ..> LanguageContext : t()
KitchenConfigurationEditorPage ..> configurationJson
configurationJson ..> ParseResult
configurationJson ..> ImportedFile
KitchenConfigurationListPage ..> kitchenConfigurationApi
KitchenConfigurationEditorPage ..> kitchenConfigurationApi
KitchenConfigurationDetailPage ..> kitchenConfigurationApi
ActivationConfirmDialog ..> ConfirmDialog
DeleteConfirmDialog ..> ConfirmDialog
KitchenConfigurationListPage ..> LoadingIndicator
KitchenConfigurationEditorPage ..> FeedbackMessage
ValidationIssueList ..> ApiError : reads details

@enduml
